        "v": 5,
        "title": "Bun v1.2.12, CI matrix refactor, evals concurrency",
        "summary": "CI pipeline switched to Bun v1.2.12 and refactored into Build/Test jobs using matrix strategy for npm-app, backend, and common packages. Evals workflow timeout increased to 360 minutes and command updated to `bun run-eval-set --concurrency 1`. `.bin/bun` script logic changed to `doesnt_need_secrets` with explicit command allowlisting for install/init/run. `.envrc` now committed directly instead of copied from example.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T12:56:54.083Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When a developer on your computer runs a local test of an agent's tool results (the pieces of information the agent sends back to its brain), the system now forwards the exact error message returned by the tool straight back into the conversation, so the agent sees what actually broke instead of a generic failure. This only affects developers actively editing and running the tool-call test files in their own terminal today; there is no visible change for end users or in any deployed feature. The test suite is the only place this new forwarding behavior is wired up right now, so until more tests or code start reading that forwarded message, it exists in the codebase but does nothing beyond the single test path. You would only notice this change if you are one of the developers opening the",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "94e48b4afa70",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:11:34.298Z"
