        "v": 5,
        "title": "Hide unused agents from @ menu",
        "summary": "Added `hidden: true` flags to `The Planner` and `Sketch` agents in `common/src/constants/agents.ts`. `UNIQUE_AGENT_NAMES` now filters out personas with the `hidden` property before mapping to display names. This prevents internal or experimental agents from appearing in the CLI `@` autocomplete menu.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T12:56:25.747Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you open the command-line assistant and type an @ symbol to pick an agent, you will no longer see entries called Sketch and The Planner in the dropdown menu. Those two agents are still built into the software, but the menu now hides them so they cannot be selected. This only affects the list that pops up during the @ autocomplete; everything else about the agents remains unchanged.",
