        "v": 5,
        "title": "Refactor tool definitions to separate files",
        "summary": "Tool definitions moved from monolithic `backend/src/tools.ts` to individual files in `backend/src/tools/definitions/`. New `backend/src/tools/constants.ts` aggregates definitions and exports `codebuffTools` map. Imports updated to use `@codebuff/common/constants/tools` for `ToolName` and `toolNames`, removing local `TOOL_LIST` dependency. Internal `AGENT_NAMES` lookup replaced with `agentTemplates` access.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T13:03:37.743Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant's available tools (like searching code, running commands, spawning sub-agents) used to all live in one big file, and now each tool has been split out into its own file so the system is easier to maintain and extend. If you watched the assistant work today, you wouldn't see any difference in what it can do or how fast it responds - this is purely behind-the-scenes housekeeping that reorganizes the code without changing behavior. The team also tidied up how the assistant looks up which tools each type of helper agent is allowed to use, pulling that information from a shared, central location instead of a local list that each part of the system used to carry around.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "0c84f1ecc4ff",
